WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.680
- I think people expect
me to be quite strict.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:03.513
- Yeah, you're not.

00:00:03.513 --> 00:00:06.700
- And stuff like that, but
I'm not really like that.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.503
- Mum's more like the
strict one, even now.

00:00:09.503 --> 00:00:10.668
- There you go, it's on camera.

00:00:10.668 --> 00:00:11.501
(laughs)

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:12.334
Documented.

00:00:13.677 --> 00:00:16.260
(gentle music)

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.870
Growing up in London is definitely

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.000
a unique experience in the UK.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.010
But then saying that,
growing up in Peckham

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.480
is unique to the London experience.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.720
It is important that I come here.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.371
It's important that...

00:00:34.371 --> 00:00:36.240
See what I mean I still communicate

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.380
with the people around here and whatever.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.420
Just to keep myself grounded.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.633
This is Peckham man,
like this is home home.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.090
The love that people
have got for each other,

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:49.090
it's a community vibe here 100%.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:51.203
So I like the fact that you know,

00:00:51.203 --> 00:00:53.103
it's still kept some of those values.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.463
What you saying

00:00:55.463 --> 00:00:56.890
- I know your boy Ricky as well.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:57.731
- Yeah yeah, cool.

00:00:57.731 --> 00:00:58.630
- My brethren still.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:00.220
- Yeah, see you later bro.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:03.430
Peckham shaped the
early stages of my life.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.240
That's where I went to school first,

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:08.750
It's where I made my first friends,

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.950
and also where my family had started.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.895
Well, this is my son by the way.

00:01:13.895 --> 00:01:14.964
Paniro.

00:01:14.964 --> 00:01:15.797
- Hi.

00:01:15.797 --> 00:01:17.282
- Paniro Walters.

00:01:17.282 --> 00:01:19.133
- He is my son, he's not my big brother.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:20.853
- You know front line though yeah?

00:01:20.853 --> 00:01:22.093
- Yeah I remember this area.

00:01:22.093 --> 00:01:23.560
I remember this.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.060
You shot the video round there innit?

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.037
- Alright, yes, so
- Yeah, the video.

00:01:27.037 --> 00:01:27.870
- When you was about two.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.410
- Yeah something like that.
- Two or something.

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:31.860
We shot a video right outside the library.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.800
South side all stars.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.270
Nicky S and Nike.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:36.103
What did I have?

00:01:36.103 --> 00:01:39.480
I had on a money T-shirt
with the red sleeves

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.520
and my red do-rag.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:41.450
- Yeah I remember that as well.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.400
- And you were a baby.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.400
You were in my arms.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:45.990
This is where you used to go down.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.870
If it was going down, this
is where it would go down.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:52.970
That off license there
with the big E on it

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:54.920
is called Cracker Jack.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.663
That was where stuff used to happen.

00:01:57.663 --> 00:01:59.286
That's all I'm saying.

00:01:59.286 --> 00:02:00.515
(laughs)

00:02:00.515 --> 00:02:02.010
(piano music)

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:05.760
Peckham has always had
that reputation of being,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.360
you know, when it came to
territories and whatever,

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.120
one of the hardest places.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.630
So when I was growing up,
there was none of this there.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:15.930
But back in the day this was rough man.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.478
- What, even this part here?

00:02:17.478 --> 00:02:18.490
- Yeah.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.230
I never saw it the way the rest of London

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.560
probably look at it.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.139
It was home to me.

00:02:25.139 --> 00:02:28.300
(ambient music)

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.450
There's a lot of really
brilliant, talented people

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.170
that come from Peckham.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.780
You got John Boyega.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.380
You got Giggs.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.020
All doing tremendously well.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.450
So it wasn't just me that benefited

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:43.453
from the intense
experience of living here.

00:02:44.307 --> 00:02:45.450
And if you can see over there,

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.350
a yellow brick estate.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.402
That's where I used to hang out.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.670
And just a few people that I grew up with

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.114
used to live there so.

00:02:52.114 --> 00:02:55.684
But it's one of the most
infamous estates in Peckham.

00:02:55.684 --> 00:02:58.601
(calm synth music)

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.680
But when I was growing up,

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.060
it was like you had to
know the right people

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.030
to come in here.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.330
You couldn't just come in.

00:03:08.394 --> 00:03:10.744
Obviously being my age
now, it's probably still

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.900
risky to be walking
around here or whatever

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:18.223
but I spent many, many a days
messing about round here.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.673
It's just life man.

00:03:22.673 --> 00:03:25.590
(calm synth music)

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.840
When I got into my early teens,

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.310
or maybe just a bit before

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.780
and I actually started
hanging out on the ends,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.940
I was kind of spending my
weekends doing stage school.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.230
I was in Sylvia Young,

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.027
doing tap, ballet, and stuff like that.

00:03:42.027 --> 00:03:43.200
(laughs)

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.393
I led a double life.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.710
You can see by the area straight away,

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:50.846
I mean, It's nothing like Peckham.

00:03:50.846 --> 00:03:51.679
Do you know what I mean?

00:03:51.679 --> 00:03:56.033
So just coming out and seeing
the size of the buildings,

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:01.240
the suited and booted
people walking up and down,

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.240
it's just different.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.470
I don't know if you can see it from here,

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.940
that's what used to be Sylvia Young's.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.950
It's where I developed my hunger.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.260
You know what I mean?

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:16.903
My passion for what I do now.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.880
You know, going to theater
school at a really young age,

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.340
compared to my peers and
people I was growing up with,

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.660
they never got those sort of experiences.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.553
I had that added kind of push.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.203
My mum, she was a huge inspiration for me.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.300
- I knew Ashley was gonna be
a success from very early on.

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:41.993
Whilst I wasn't really 100%,

00:04:41.993 --> 00:04:44.950
even 50%, or even 30%

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.970
happy about you doing
the Soul Solid stuff,

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.686
I knew you were talented in that as well.

00:04:50.686 --> 00:04:53.494
(dead phone line buzzing)

00:04:53.494 --> 00:04:56.661
(drum and bass music)

00:04:59.677 --> 00:05:00.980
- Getting into Soul Solid

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:03.600
initially wasn't even about music for me.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.170
It was about being a part of something,

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:08.217
and being able to identify
with another group of people

00:05:08.217 --> 00:05:10.340
that were the same.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.210
To be fair, I was quite shy you know.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.410
'cause what you gotta understand is,

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.820
everyone had grown up together.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:19.070
So I wasn't a part of that

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:21.800
'cause I came from
Peckham, and when I joined,

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.120
these guys had obviously all had years

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:25.253
of growing up together so.

00:05:25.253 --> 00:05:27.163
I think it took me a while to kind of,

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.040
to warm into it.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.300
You know what I mean?

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.381
- Do you remember that time?

00:05:31.381 --> 00:05:32.214
(mumbling together)

00:05:32.214 --> 00:05:34.120
- We were on a coach innit? On a coach.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.150
And I was sitting next to him,

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.100
and the guy started freestyling,

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.580
just from the top of his head.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:39.960
And I was like, "what?",

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.020
'cause I never heard him rap before.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:42.853
And from that point,

00:05:42.853 --> 00:05:44.545
I was like, "I'm rolling with you."

00:05:44.545 --> 00:05:45.378
(laughs)

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:46.530
and we were writing together,

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:47.690
he was producing for me,

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:49.190
writing with me and stuff like that.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:51.632
You know from that point,
me and Swiss hit it off.

00:05:51.632 --> 00:05:52.940
(synth music)

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:55.010
I grew up as a lonely child.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:57.560
I think a part of me
was always looking for

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:01.913
a family, or a gang, or
siblings, or whatever.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.660
But what I realized was,
being around Soul Solid,

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:08.530
they were all very family
orientated as well.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:10.370
We all just wanted to make sure that

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.413
we were all alright together.

00:06:14.004 --> 00:06:15.490
Battersea at that time, you know,

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:17.033
it was a home away from home.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.500
- We come from a family kind of basis

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.740
when it comes to the
people that we're around,

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.100
and the circle that we're in.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.630
So we make everyone
feel like they're home.

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:32.960
You come to our house,
you eat Sunday dinner,

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:34.450
you meet our families.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:35.283
Do you get what I'm saying?

00:06:35.283 --> 00:06:36.810
And we treat you like family so,

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:38.840
hence the name Soul Solid.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:41.030
- Every day, being in
a part of Soul Solid,

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:42.497
and having so many people around you,

00:06:42.497 --> 00:06:44.110
who were acting as role models,

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:46.450
mentors, friends, or whatever,

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:51.433
It's just all round a big
important part of our lives.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:54.029
- People still living here.

00:06:54.029 --> 00:06:55.179
(laughs)
Fucking hell.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:58.223
- What floor was it?

00:06:58.223 --> 00:07:00.650
- I think it was fourth
floor or something.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:02.030
- Ah I remember this block.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:02.863
- Yeah.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.720
So this is the block
where the lighter from

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:06.660
radio station was.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.430
I think it was on the fourth floor.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:09.710
- Remember we were...

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.330
Obviously there was a
garage scene before us,

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:13.710
but the music that we were doing

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:16.885
and how we were kind of
changing it, it was new.

00:07:16.885 --> 00:07:18.750
(synth music)

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:22.800
So what radio became for us was

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:24.920
a practice ground.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.350
You were owning your craft all the time.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:31.640
We could still be underground
guys from Battersea now,

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.613
if we never started our
own pirate radio station.

00:07:36.669 --> 00:07:39.169
(synth music)

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:42.890
I think it's easy to trap yourself.

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:46.370
It's easy to feel like coming from

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:50.550
that socially kind of deprived place,

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:53.290
It's easy to feel negative all the time.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.410
It's easy to feel like
everyone's against you,

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:58.190
and the world's against
you and whatever but,

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:00.620
actually I just wanted more.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.620
(bass guitar music)

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:09.469
I've always understood the power of me.

00:08:09.469 --> 00:08:11.430
(bass guitar music)

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:13.201
Being in the position I am.

00:08:13.201 --> 00:08:15.890
(bass guitar music)

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:19.088
The legacy is about how many
people you inspire really.

00:08:19.088 --> 00:08:20.800
(bass guitar music)

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.350
That's a great thing to be
a part of, that journey.

00:08:24.609 --> 00:08:27.000
(upbeat music)

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.740
Having a dream, having a goal,

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.433
what you wanna make of your
life or whatever is great,

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:36.626
but your foundation is your foundation.

00:08:36.626 --> 00:08:37.890
(laughs)

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:40.528
That's what it's gonna prepare you for.

00:08:40.528 --> 00:08:43.239
For all of the opportunities
that you're given

00:08:43.239 --> 00:08:44.200
in the future.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:46.600
You always have to remember
where you come from.

00:08:48.206 --> 00:08:49.039
(disk scratch)

